/-!
# A lower bound for the four generated centralizer words

The checked orbit trees for the successive stabilizers of points 0 and 1
reach 840 and 96 different points. A further word fixes both and sends 2
to 645. Disjoint cosets therefore give 840 · 96 · 2 = 161280 elements in
the subgroup generated by the four literal words. Generation of the full
centralizer is not assumed: that needs the separate upper bound.

The tables are packed candidate data, and all injectivity, fixed-point and
orbit-edge assertions are checked by kernel reduction. The 840-edge decision
is split into 32-edge declarations to bound compiler memory.

Source: the unchanged ATLAS HeG1-p2058B0 action and the Bray-search words in
`Source/discovery.json`; `Source/discover_lower.py` reproduces the orbit data.
-/

public section
